efore  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\mathcal K_n=\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n-1\\}} .\n\\]\n\nIn words: for every integer \\(n\\ge 3\\) the possible numbers of sunny lines in a configuration of \\(n\\) distinct lines covering all points \\((a,b)\\) with \\(a,b\\ge1\\) and \\(a+b\\le n+1\\) are exactly the integers from \\(0\\) up to \\(n-1\\).  \n\n--- \n\n**Self‑Correction Instruction**  \nThe solution above is self‑contained, each claim is proved, and the logical flow follows the outline given in the summary. All mathematical expressions are typeset in TeX, and the final answer is presented in the required \\(\\boxed{}\\) format. No extraneous commentary is included."
